    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c3d9bf0_78b0654d",
        "filename": "Tethering/common/TetheringLib/src/android/net/TetheringManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1440,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T10:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just rename to unpackBits which probably more reusable for tethering.\n\nHere are the reasons that I don\u0027t want to using native array and BitUtils.\n1. Giving that we already use bitmap in server side, covert it to native array then pass to client side seems redundant. No matter what we need to cover it to a set because the surface of API \"onSupportedTetheringTypes(@NonNull Set\u003cInteger\u003e supportedTypes)\". We can covert bitmap to a set directly instead of covering bitamp to native array then cover it to a set.\n2. BitUtils is a @hide class in bootclass path and it non-updatable code and it don\u0027t support unpackBits to a set.\n3. Giving I need to unpack bit in bootclass path class and it just a simple util. I\u0027d prefer just add this util directly here instead of link a new class which include more methods that tethering don\u0027t need to use because proguard don\u0027t enable in framework-xxxx.jar libraries.",
      "parentUuid": "dac80b4b_a049c833",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1438,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1440,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "641348da936d2de8119b43b56d975f227cca13d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "650559ea_4d92a09e",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-04T15:30:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AIDL supports integers and integer arrays just fine. See for example Parcel#writeIntArray.\n\nFor equality, you can use com.android.internal.util.ArrayUtils#equals.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 282,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 282,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "641348da936d2de8119b43b56d975f227cca13d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f452be6d_5036e8b6",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T10:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, AIDL supports primitive int array but don\u0027t support Integer object array. I don\u0027t want to covert the bitmap to primitive int array. The API surface is Set\u003cInteger\u003e, the value copy between primitive int array and Integer set is annoy. \n\nIf I understand the suggestion here correctly, it would be:\nhave a Parcelable object and it would encapsulate the parcel. In server side covert bitmap to native array and writeToParcel then pass the parcel Parcelable object to client side. In client side, use createFromParcel and covert native array to set.",
      "parentUuid": "650559ea_4d92a09e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 282,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 282,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "641348da936d2de8119b43b56d975f227cca13d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
