      "writtenOn": "2022-03-04T15:30:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This call only works on T though, right? Because updateSupportedDownstreams only updates the bitmap with Ethernet if isAtleastT()? If so, that\u0027s wrong - this test should run on R+.\n\nMaybe what you could do is:\n\n- Ensure updateSupportedDownstreams always populates all the downstreams correctly\n- Make the new callback correct in all cases (i.e., always reports Ethernet, p2p, ncm, etc. correctly, even on R and S)\n- Make old callback, and isTetheringSupported, ignore all bits in the bitmap that didn\u0027t matter on R and S (i.e., ncm, p2p, ethernet)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 175,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "641348da936d2de8119b43b56d975f227cca13d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1bc3592_8d14cba3",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/integration/src/android/net/EthernetTetheringTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T10:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, this should also be able to run before T. Before T, updateSupportedDownstreams would update Ethernet if any of wifi, usb and bt is not disabled.\n\nI think we need to keep consistency between old API(old callback and isTetheringSupported) and new callback. For R and S, it would be very strange that the caller get the new callback says ethernet is supported but start ethernet tethering fail because of isTetheringSupported is false (and no UI). Or make start ethernet tethering work while isTetheringSupported is false also be very weird.\n\nThe behavior would be:\n    - For R and S: if wifi, usb, bluetooth are all disabled, updateSupportedDownstreams would populates zero supported tethering type. And both old/new callback and isTetheringSupported would have same behavior. If one of wifi, usb bluetooth type is enabled, updateSupportedDownstreams populates all the downstreams correctly.\n    - After T, updateSupportedDownstreams always populates all the downstreams correctly.\n    \nI don\u0027t change any behavior in this test. Before this change, R and S ethernet tethering would also not be supported if wifi, usb and bluetooth are disabled.",
      "parentUuid": "cade5564_22a574c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 175,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 48
      },
